swift-pii bundles data derived from several third-party projects. Each is
listed below with its licence and where it lives in this repository.

This project is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by any of them.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Presidio — MIT
Copyright (c) Presidio Contributors
https://github.com/data-privacy-stack/presidio

Regex patterns, context word lists, score constants, entity type names and test
expectations are derived from Presidio. MIT permits this; attribution is to
"Presidio Contributors" rather than Microsoft, following the project's own
LICENSE after its move to the data-privacy-stack organisation.

  Sources/PresidioRecognizers/Resources/recognizers.json
  Sources/PresidioRecognizers/Resources/recognizer_data.json
  Sources/PresidioRecognizers/Resources/iban_countries.json
  Tests/PresidioConformance/Fixtures/*.json

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Public Suffix List — Mozilla Public License 2.0
https://publicsuffix.org/

Used by the email recognizer to identify registrable domains. MPL-2.0 is
file-level copyleft, so the list is kept in its own file with the upstream
notice preserved rather than merged into the MIT-licensed data around it. IDN
suffixes are punycoded at extraction time; the transformation is in
Tools/extract_recognizer_data.py.

  Sources/PresidioRecognizers/Resources/public_suffix_list.json

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
libphonenumber — Apache License 2.0
Copyright (C) 2009 The Libphonenumber Authors
https://github.com/google/libphonenumber

Phone number metadata and the matcher's own regular expressions, obtained via
the python-phonenumbers port (also Apache-2.0). The parsing, validation and
matching algorithms in Sources/PresidioRecognizers/PhoneNumber*.swift are ported
from that implementation.

  Sources/PresidioRecognizers/Resources/phone_metadata.json

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
spaCy and spacy-lookups-data — MIT
Copyright (c) ExplosionAI GmbH
https://github.com/explosion/spaCy
https://github.com/explosion/spacy-lookups-data

The English tokenizer's prefix/suffix/infix rules and special cases, and the
lexeme_norm table. The tokenizer implementation in Sources/PresidioNLP is
ported from spaCy.

Note: spacy-lookups-data also ships WordNet-derived lemma tables under the
WordNet 3.0 licence. Those are NOT bundled here — only lexeme_norm is — so no
WordNet attribution is required.

  Sources/PresidioNLP/Resources/en_tokenizer.json

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Unicode Character Database — Unicode License
Copyright (c) 1991-2024 Unicode, Inc.
https://www.unicode.org/copyright.html

Character-class membership tables (\w, \d, \s) generated from Python's `regex`
module, which derives them from the UCD. Generated by
Tools/unicode_classes_python.py and pinned so behaviour cannot drift with the
host platform's Unicode version.

  Sources/PresidioRegex/UnicodeTables.swift

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
spaCy models (en_core_web_sm / en_core_web_lg) — MIT
Copyright (c) ExplosionAI GmbH

NOT bundled. SpacyNER loads them from a path at runtime. Noted here because the
NER implementation reads their thinc weight format directly, and because their
LICENSES_SOURCES records OntoNotes 5 as "commercial (licensed by Explosion)" —
an obligation discharged upstream that does not propagate to users of the
weights.
